TITLE:: SequencePlayer
SUMMARY:: Plays a sequence of notes from PianoRoll.
RELATED:: Classes/PianoRoll, Classes/Sequencer

DESCRIPTION::
Allows a set of notes displayed in a LINK::Classes/PianoRoll::, for example which has just been recorded from a keyboard, to be played back.

NOTE::
You can run the unit tests for TELETYPE::Sequencer:: by running:
CODE::
(
UnitTest.reportPasses_(false);
SequencePlayerUnitTests.run;
)
::
::


CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a new TELETYPE::SequencePlayer::.

ARGUMENT:: tempoClock
The clock used to schedule playback. Defaults to TempoClock.default.

ARGUMENT:: midiOut
The MIDI output device. Defaults to Setup.midi.

ARGUMENT:: sequencer
An optional LINK::Classes/Sequencer::. When supplied, LINK::#-play:: and LINK::#-stop:: acquire and release that sequencer's shared playback clock. CODE::nil:: keeps the clock passed as CODE::tempoClock::.

returns:: A new TELETYPE::SequencePlayer:: instance.


INSTANCEMETHODS::
PRIVATE:: prResetPlayingNotes

METHOD:: delta
The beat length of each playback slice (the scheduling grid quant).

returns:: The slice duration in beats (0.0625 by default).

METHOD:: init
Initialises a new TELETYPE::SequencePlayer::.

ARGUMENT:: tempoClock
The clock used to schedule playback. Defaults to TempoClock.default.

ARGUMENT:: midiOut
The MIDI output device. Defaults to Setup.midi.

ARGUMENT:: sequencer
An optional LINK::Classes/Sequencer::. When supplied, LINK::#-play:: and LINK::#-stop:: acquire and release that sequencer's shared playback clock. CODE::nil:: keeps the clock passed as CODE::tempoClock::.

returns:: This instance.

METHOD:: isPlaying
CODE::true:: after LINK::#-play:: until LINK::#-stop::. This becomes false as soon as stop is called, before the final slice sends note-offs.

RETURNS::
CODE::true:: while playback is in progress.

METHOD:: latency
The scheduling offset applied to MIDI events, in beats.

returns:: The current latency value in beats (0.01 by default).

METHOD:: loopEnd
The loop end time in beats.

returns:: The current loop end time.

METHOD:: loopStart
The loop start time in beats.

returns:: The current loop start time.

METHOD:: midiChannel
The MIDI channel used for note on/off messages.

returns:: The current MIDI channel.

METHOD:: onPlayheadMove_
Registers a function called each time the playhead advances during playback. The function receives the start beat of the current slice. The callback is scheduled on the tempo clock after LINK::Classes/MIDIOut:: latency so the visible playhead stays aligned with heard MIDI.

ARGUMENT:: action
A LINK::Classes/Function:: invoked when the playhead moves to the start of the next slice.

METHOD:: alignPlayhead
Moves the playhead to the nearest point on a Sync-to grid that has the same offset into that grid as CODE::beat::. The loop start is local beat 0, and distance is the shorter way around the loop. When two points are equally close, the one forward from the playhead is chosen. Does not start playback.

ARGUMENT:: syncTo
An integer from 1 to 16. The grid size in beats.

ARGUMENT:: beat
The clock beat used to read the offset, CODE::beat.mod(syncTo)::.

RETURNS::
The playhead time after the snap, in beats.

METHOD:: play
Starts playback from the current playhead position on the next whole beat of the tempo clock. If the clock is already on a beat, playback starts immediately. Slices after that stay on the slice grid. When this player was constructed with a LINK::Classes/Sequencer::, this acquires that sequencer's shared clock and LINK::#-stop:: releases it. When CODE::syncTo:: is supplied, the playhead is snapped before the first slice. Otherwise the playhead is not rewritten from the clock.

ARGUMENT:: tempoClock
An optional LINK::Classes/TempoClock:: for this run. When omitted, playback uses the clock passed to LINK::#*new::, or LINK::Classes/TempoClock::.default when that was CODE::nil::. Ignored when this player was constructed with a LINK::Classes/Sequencer::. That player uses the sequencer's shared clock instead.

ARGUMENT:: startImmediately
When CODE::true::, plays the first slice now. Defaults to CODE::false::. Without a LINK::Classes/Sequencer::, also sets the clock to beat 0. With a sequencer, the shared clock is set to beat 0 only when this play creates it.

ARGUMENT:: startNow
When CODE::true::, plays the first slice now and leaves the clock's beat unchanged. Defaults to CODE::false::.

ARGUMENT:: syncTo
An optional integer from 1 to 16. When supplied, the playhead snaps onto that grid using the clock beat after the clock is chosen, and the playhead-move callback is called with that time before the first slice. CODE::nil:: leaves the playhead where it is.

RETURNS::
A report string from the first playback slice when playback starts immediately. Otherwise CODE::nil::, because the first slice is still waiting for the beat.

METHOD:: playheadTime
The current playback position in beats. Set with TELETYPE::playheadTime_::.

returns:: The current playhead time in beats.

METHOD:: sequence
The array of LINK::Classes/PlayableNote:: instances to play.

returns:: The current sequence.

METHOD:: stop
Stops playback. Note-offs for sounding notes are sent on the next slice. When this player was constructed with a LINK::Classes/Sequencer::, that slice then releases this player's hold on the shared clock. When CODE::onStopped:: is supplied, that function runs once after those note-offs and after the release.

ARGUMENT:: onStopped
An optional LINK::Classes/Function::. Called once from the final slice, after note-offs and after a sequencer-backed player releases the shared clock.


